the village wells dried up,
and the river turned to sand.

267
00:25:50,815 --> 00:25:52,639
The crops were
swallowed by the earth,

268
00:25:52,726 --> 00:25:55,860
and the animals laid down
and turned to dust.

269
00:25:57,263 --> 00:25:59,279
Then one night there was
a fire in the fields.

270
00:26:01,045 --> 00:26:02,646
The men went out
to fight the fire.

271
00:26:03,323 --> 00:26:05,985
When they came back, the women were
crying in the darkness.

272
00:26:12,765 --> 00:26:13,993
[SPEAKS FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

273
00:26:17,191 --> 00:26:18,259
Children.

274
00:26:19,914 --> 00:26:21,958
He says they stole
their children.

275
00:26:27,958 --> 00:26:31,707
- [CLINKING]
- [CROWS CAWING]

276
00:26:39,914 --> 00:26:42,536
[PANTING]

277
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:14,185
Sankara! Sankara...

278
00:27:18,001 --> 00:27:19,201
WOMAN: [SHOUTING] Ranjit!

279
00:27:20,843 --> 00:27:21,887
Ranjit!

280
00:27:22,017 --> 00:27:28,903
[CRYING]

281
00:27:47,957 --> 00:27:49,045
Sankara.

282
00:28:02,641 --> 00:28:03,929
[PANTING]

283
00:28:05,334 --> 00:28:08,684
Little boy escaped
from the evil palace.

284
00:28:09,969 --> 00:28:12,590
Many other children
still there.

285
00:28:12,677 --> 00:28:14,244
What we do, Dr. Jones?

286
00:28:22,905 --> 00:28:24,080
What you think?

287
00:28:25,731 --> 00:28:29,702
I think that somebody believes the
good luck rock from this village

288
00:28:30,539 --> 00:28:32,784
is one of
the lost Sankara Stones.

289
00:28:32,871 --> 00:28:34,003
What is Sankara?

290
00:28:35,905 --> 00:28:37,398
Fortune and glory, kid.

291
00:28:39,356 --> 00:28:41,155
Fortune and glory.

292
00:28:55,210 --> 00:28:57,681
[GRUNTING]

293
00:29:05,087 --> 00:29:08,470
Willie, quit monkeying around
on that thing.

294
00:29:14,435 --> 00:29:15,887
[SPEAKS FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

295
00:29:16,321 --> 00:29:17,369
[TRUMPETING]

296
00:29:17,426 --> 00:29:19,614
Oh, wait a second! Indy!

297
00:29:19,701 --> 00:29:21,773
I can't go to Delhi
like this!

298
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:25,612
We're not going to Delhi, doll.
We're going to Pankot Palace.

299
00:29:26,229 --> 00:29:27,429
Pankot?

300
00:29:27,506 --> 00:29:30,051
I can't go to Pankot!
I'm a singer.

301
00:29:30,178 --> 00:29:32,714
Oh, I need to call my agent.
Is there a phone?

302
00:29:32,801 --> 00:29:34,063
Anybody, I need a phone!

303
00:29:37,495 --> 00:29:43,943
[PRAYING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

304
00:30:03,202 --> 00:30:04,525
[SNIFFS]

305
00:30:08,669 --> 00:30:09,738
[SNIFFS]

306
00:30:09,825 --> 00:30:11,661
[GROANS IN DISGUST]

307
00:30:23,620 --> 00:30:25,119
[TRUMPETING]

308
00:30:25,196 --> 00:30:27,442
Oh, quit complaining.
This is expensive stuff.

309
00:30:30,124 --> 00:30:32,642
You come to America with me,
and we get job in circus.

310
00:30:32,729 --> 00:30:34,775
You like that?
You like America?

311
00:30:34,862 --> 00:30:36,335
You're my best friend.

312
00:30:36,962 --> 00:30:38,577
- You're my best friend.
- [SPEAKS FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

313
00:30:40,084 --> 00:30:42,325
WILLIE: What big birds!

314
00:30:42,847 --> 00:30:45,278
Those aren't big birds,
sweetheart.

315
00:30:45,405 --> 00:30:47,947
They're giant
vampire bats.

316
00:30:48,798 --> 00:30:49,925
Bats?

317
00:30:57,624 --> 00:30:58,743
[TRUMPETS]

318
00:30:59,110 --> 00:31:01,713
Pipe down, you big baboon.
This doesn't hurt.

319
00:31:01,780 --> 00:31:05,138
You know what you really need?
You really need a bath.

320
00:31:09,736 --> 00:31:12,160
[SOBBING]

321
00:31:14,464 --> 00:31:16,246
[LAUGHING] Ha-ha, very funny.

322
00:31:17,644 --> 00:31:18,811
Very funny.

323
00:31:19,994 --> 00:31:21,198
Very funny.

324
00:31:21,604 --> 00:31:22,752
All wet.

325
00:31:24,073 --> 00:31:26,724
WILLIE:
I was happy in Shanghai.

326
00:31:27,779 --> 00:31:30,571
I had a little house
and a garden.

327
00:31:30,648 --> 00:31:32,310
[MOSQUITO BUZZES]

328
00:31:32,397 --> 00:31:35,716
My friends were rich. We went to parties
all the time in limousines.

329
00:31:35,813 --> 00:31:38,142
I hate being outside!

330
00:31:38,229 --> 00:31:40,966
[CRYING]

331
00:31:41,044 --> 00:31:43,886
I'm a singer!
I could lose my voice!

332
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:48,588
I think we'll
camp here tonight.

333
00:31:50,764 --> 00:31:51,852
Cut it out.

334
00:31:58,353 --> 00:32:00,446
- What do you got?
- Two sixes.

335
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:03,036
Aha-ha, three aces.
I win.

336
00:32:03,133 --> 00:32:07,420
[LAUGHING] Two more game,
I have all your money.

337
00:32:08,027 --> 00:32:10,340
It's poker, Shorty,
anything can happen.

338
00:32:11,267 --> 00:32:13,351
Where did you find
your little bodyguard?

339
00:32:13,838 --> 00:32:15,626
I didn't find him,
I caught him.

340
00:32:16,253 --> 00:32:17,438
What?

341
00:32:17,615 --> 00:32:20,689
Shorty's family were killed
when the Japanese bombed Shanghai.

342
00:32:20,786 --> 00:32:22,618
He's been living on the streets
since he was four.

343
00:32:22,686 --> 00:32:26,074
I caught him trying to pick my pocket,
didn't I, short stuff?

344
00:32:26,171 --> 00:32:29,771
- [SCREECHING]
- [SCREAMING]

345
00:32:29,855 --> 00:32:32,222
Biggest trouble
with her is the noise.

346
00:32:37,530 --> 00:32:40,172
[SCREAMING CONTINUES]

347
00:32:40,259 --> 00:32:43,323
Hey! You cheat,
Dr. Jones. You cheat!

348
00:32:43,430 --> 00:32:44,948
- What do you mean?
- You take four card.

349
00:32:45,035 --> 00:32:47,354
- [GIBBERING]
- [SCREAMING]

350
00:32:47,441 --> 00:32:48,723
- You pay now.
- Oh, they were stuck together.

351
00:32:48,820 --> 00:32:50,314
- No stuck. No mistake.
- They were stuck together.

352
00:32:50,371 --> 00:32:53,307
- It's a mistake.
- I'm very little. You cheat very big.

353
00:32:53,414 --> 00:32:54,915
[HISSING]

354
00:32:55,002 --> 00:32:56,433
Dr. Jones, you cheat!

355
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:58,285
You pay money.
You owe me ten cent.

356
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:01,083
Look at this. Look at this.

357
00:33:01,675 --> 00:33:03,848
- [HOOTING]
- [SCREAMING]

358
00:33:03,945 --> 00:33:05,978
You accuse me of cheating.
You're cheating.

359
00:33:06,075 --> 00:33:07,754
[BOTH SPEAKING CHINESE]

360
00:33:11,453 --> 00:33:12,759
[CROAKING]

361
00:33:12,846 --> 00:33:15,152
You make me poor. No fun.

362
00:33:15,239 --> 00:33:16,806
Play with you no fun.

363
00:33:16,893 --> 00:33:18,015
I quit.

364
00:33:18,452 --> 00:33:19,767
I quit, too.

365
00:33:20,054 --> 00:33:21,974
This place is
completely surrounded.

366
00:33:22,051 --> 00:33:24,363
The entire place is crawling
with living things.

367
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:26,062
That's why they call it
the jungle, sweetheart.

368
00:33:26,149 --> 00:33:27,885
- [ROARING]
- Oh, my God, what else is out there?

369
00:33:27,982 --> 00:33:29,123
Willie, wait...

370
00:33:29,210 --> 00:33:30,750
[SCREAMS]

371
00:33:35,129 --> 00:33:36,337
Willie, Willie...

372
00:33:36,984 --> 00:33:38,708
What is that? Is that short
for something?

373
00:33:40,105 --> 00:33:43,607
"Willie" is my
professional name, Indiana.

374
00:33:43,944 --> 00:33:46,446
Hey, lady, you call him
Dr. Jones.

375
00:33:46,653 --> 00:33:48,229
My professional name.

376
00:33:50,454 --> 00:33:53,016
Why are you dragging us off
to this deserted palace?

377
00:33:53,103 --> 00:33:54,497
Fortune and glory?

378
00:33:54,844 --> 00:33:56,012
Fortune and glory.

379
00:33:57,194 --> 00:33:58,805
Well...

380
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:02,406
this is a piece of
an old manuscript.

381
00:34:03,356 --> 00:34:05,986
This pictograph
represents Sankara,

382
00:34:06,073 --> 00:34:07,329
- a priest.
- Scram.

383
00:34:08,396 --> 00:34:11,099
Gentle. Gentle.
This is hundreds of years old.

384
00:34:11,186 --> 00:34:12,688
Is that some kind
of writing?

385
00:34:12,775 --> 00:34:14,267
Yeah, it's Sanskrit.

386
00:34:14,475 --> 00:34:15,484
Cut it out.

387
00:34:15,581 --> 00:34:17,383
It's part of
the legend of Sankara.

388
00:34:18,231 --> 00:34:21,513
He climbs Mount Kalisa
where he meets Siva, the Hindu god.

389
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,119
WILLIE: That's Siva? And what's
he handing the priest?

390
00:34:25,527 --> 00:34:27,229
Rocks. Stop.

391
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:30,352
He told him to go
forth and combat evil.

392
00:34:30,889 --> 00:34:34,727
And to help him, he gave him five
sacred stones with magical properties.

393
00:34:35,145 --> 00:34:36,799
Magic rocks?

394
00:34:36,886 --> 00:34:40,673
My grandpa was a magician. He spent his
entire life with a rabbit in his pocket

395
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:41,773
and pigeons up his sleeves.

396
00:34:41,850 --> 00:34:44,818
He made a lot of children happy
and died a very poor man.

397
00:34:45,286 --> 00:34:47,996
Magic rocks.
Fortune and glory.

398
00:34:48,193 --> 00:34:49,856
Sweet dreams,
Dr. Jones.

399
00:34:51,118 --> 00:34:52,223
Where are you going?

400
00:34:52,910 --> 00:34:55,171
I'd sleep closer,
if I were you.

401
00:34:56,084 --> 00:34:57,322
For safety's sake.

402
00:34:58,139 --> 00:35:01,119
Dr. Jones, I'd be safer
sleeping with a snake.

403
00:35:01,202 --> 00:35:02,302
[HISSING]

404
00:35:03,477 --> 00:35:06,182
I said, cut it out!

405
00:35:10,136 --> 00:35:11,758
I hate that elephant.

406
00:35:40,743 --> 00:35:41,874
Indy, look!

407
00:35:43,442 --> 00:35:46,822
INDY: I see it, Shorty.
That's it. Pankot Palace.

408
00:35:59,366 --> 00:36:00,708
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

409
00:36:12,895 --> 00:36:16,722
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

410
00:37:05,322 --> 00:37:07,121
Dr. Jones, what you look at?

411
00:37:08,515 --> 00:37:09,908
Don't come up here.

412
00:37:11,968 --> 00:37:14,909
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

413
00:37:16,105 --> 00:37:18,568
WILLIE: No! No, no, no, no!
Don't leave! No!

414
00:37:18,655 --> 00:37:21,399
No, no, no, no, no!

415
00:37:21,486 --> 00:37:23,082
Oh, baby elephant,
stay here!

416
00:37:23,159 --> 00:37:25,619
Oh, no! Indy!

417
00:37:25,706 --> 00:37:27,794
They're stealing our rides!

418
00:37:28,317 --> 00:37:29,863
We walk from here.

419
00:37:34,019 --> 00:37:35,629
[CAWING AND SCREECHING]

420
00:38:06,749 --> 00:38:07,951
Hello.

421
00:38:08,328 --> 00:38:10,706
I should say you
look rather lost.

422
00:38:11,828 --> 00:38:13,986
But then I cannot imagine
where in the world

423
00:38:14,093 --> 00:38:15,670
the three of you
would look at home.

424
00:38:16,238 --> 00:38:18,370
We're not lost.
We're on our way to Delhi.

425
00:38:19,107 --> 00:38:20,302
This is Miss Scott.

426
00:38:20,979 --> 00:38:22,676
This is Mr. Round.

427
00:38:22,763 --> 00:38:24,112
Short Round.

428
00:38:24,199 --> 00:38:25,878
My name is Indiana Jones.

429
00:38:26,825 --> 00:38:29,176
Dr. Jones,
the eminent archeologist?

430
00:38:29,683 --> 00:38:31,028
Hard to believe,
isn't it?

431
00:38:32,415 --> 00:38:35,706
I remember first hearing your name
when I was up at Oxford.

432
00:38:36,723 --> 00:38:40,688
I'm Chattar Lal, Prime Minister
to His Highness, the Maharajah of Pankot.

433
00:38:42,133 --> 00:38:43,262
I'm enchanted.

434
00:38:43,489 --> 00:38:46,549
Enchanted. Thank you very much.
Thank you very much.

435
00:38:46,656 --> 00:38:48,566
Welcome to Pankot Palace!

436
00:38:52,097 --> 00:38:53,371
Enchanted, huh?

437
00:39:01,106 --> 00:39:05,164
[INDIAN MUSIC PLAYING]

438
00:39:05,271 --> 00:39:06,850
INDY:
Shorty, where's my razor?

439
00:39:08,544 --> 00:39:10,724
[SINGING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

440
00:39:25,089 --> 00:39:31,336
[INDISTINCT CHATTERING]

441
00:39:32,243 --> 00:39:36,658
We are fortunate tonight
to have so many unexpected visitors.

442
00:39:36,845 --> 00:39:38,621
This is Captain... ...Blumburtt.

443
00:39:38,708 --> 00:39:40,093
11th Poona Rifles.

444
00:39:40,370 --> 00:39:43,116
And you, sir, are
Dr. Jones, I presume.

445
00:39:43,556 --> 00:39:44,776
I am, Captain.

446
00:39:44,853 --> 00:39:48,524
Captain Blumburtt and his troops
are on a routine inspection tour.

447
00:39:48,911 --> 00:39:52,506
The British find it amusing
to inspect us at their convenience.

448
00:39:52,683 --> 00:39:57,055
I do hope, sir,
that it's not inconvenient to you, sir.

449
00:39:58,082 --> 00:40:00,828
The British worry so
about their empire.

450
00:40:00,935 --> 00:40:03,668
Makes us all feel like
well-cared-for children.

451
00:40:04,596 --> 00:40:05,645
[SCREAMS]

452
00:40:05,732 --> 00:40:07,807
[SHOUTING IN CHINESE]

453
00:40:14,178 --> 00:40:16,432
You look beautiful.

454
00:40:16,999 --> 00:40:19,459
I think the Maharajah
is swimming in loot.

455
00:40:19,546 --> 00:40:22,067
Maybe it wasn't such a bad idea
coming here after all.

456
00:40:23,224 --> 00:40:24,886
You look like a princess.

457
00:40:25,843 --> 00:40:29,262
Mr. Lal, what do they call
the Maharajah's wife?

458
00:40:29,850 --> 00:40:32,239
His Highness has
not yet taken a wife.

459
00:40:32,326 --> 00:40:33,377
How interesting.

460
00:40:33,494 --> 00:40:36,366
Well, maybe it's because
he hasn't found the right woman.

461
00:40:50,541 --> 00:40:52,472
His Supreme Highness,

462
00:40:53,652 --> 00:40:56,424
guardian of Pankot tradition,

463
00:40:57,523 --> 00:40:59,994
the Maharajah of Pankot,

464
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:03,221
Zalim Singh.

465
00:41:24,857 --> 00:41:26,593
That's the Maharajah?

466
00:41:27,077 --> 00:41:28,150
A kid?

467
00:41:31,062 --> 00:41:33,442
Maybe he like
older women.

468
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:43,828
Captain Blumburtt
was just telling me

469
00:41:43,915 --> 00:41:46,374
something of
the interesting history of the palace,

470
00:41:46,471 --> 00:41:48,278
the importance
it played in the mutiny.

471
00:41:49,125 --> 00:41:53,512
It seems the British never forget
the Mutiny of 1857.

472
00:41:53,625 --> 00:41:54,785
[LAUGHS]

473
00:41:54,872 --> 00:41:56,957
Yes, well, you know, I think
there are other events,

474
00:41:57,074 --> 00:41:59,224
before the mutiny,
going back a century,

475
00:41:59,291 --> 00:42:01,817
back to the time of Clive,
that are more interesting.

476
00:42:02,184 --> 00:42:04,445
CHATTAR:
And what events are those, Dr. Jones?

477
00:42:04,562 --> 00:42:07,735
INDY: Well, if memory serves me
correctly, this area, this province,

478
00:42:07,812 --> 00:42:10,171
was the center of activity
for the Thuggee.

479
00:42:11,730 --> 00:42:13,123
[EXCLAIMS]

480
00:42:13,210 --> 00:42:16,102
Snake... Surprise.

481
00:42:16,474 --> 00:42:17,735
What's the surprise?

482
00:42:20,027 --> 00:42:22,523
[SQUISHING]

483
00:42:27,256 --> 00:42:30,638
Dr. Jones,
you know perfectly well

484
00:42:30,705 --> 00:42:33,055
the Thuggee cult has been dead
for nearly a century.

485
00:42:33,143 --> 00:42:34,348
Yes, of course.

486
00:42:35,015 --> 00:42:36,823
The Thuggee
was an obscenity

487
00:42:37,460 --> 00:42:40,106
that worshipped Kali
with human sacrifices.

488
00:42:41,573 --> 00:42:43,153
The British Army
nicely did away with them.

489
00:42:43,656 --> 00:42:46,854
[RATTLING]

490
00:42:46,941 --> 00:42:50,169
INDY: Well, I suppose stories
of the Thuggee die hard.

491
00:42:50,266 --> 00:42:52,191
CHATTAR:
There are no stories anymore.

492
00:42:53,206 --> 00:42:54,425
INDY: I'm not so sure.

493
00:42:55,553 --> 00:42:57,275
We came from
a small village.

494
00:42:57,732 --> 00:43:01,388
The peasants there told us Pankot
Palace was growing powerful again

495
00:43:01,475 --> 00:43:03,387
because of some
ancient evil.

496
00:43:04,044 --> 00:43:05,758
Village stories,
Dr. Jones.

497
00:43:05,845 --> 00:43:08,858
They're just
fear and folklore.

498
00:43:10,476 --> 00:43:12,675
You're beginning to worry
Captain Blumburtt.

499
00:43:13,762 --> 00:43:19,419
I'm not worried,
Mr. Prime Minister, just interested.

500
00:43:21,459 --> 00:43:25,024
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

501
00:43:35,048 --> 00:43:37,855
What? You are not eating?

502
00:43:39,948 --> 00:43:41,298
I had bugs for lunch.

503
00:43:45,911 --> 00:43:46,961
Give me your hat.

504
00:43:49,253 --> 00:43:51,296
- Why?
- 'Cause I'm gonna puke in it.

505
00:43:53,134 --> 00:43:54,211
[BURPS]

506
00:43:54,308 --> 00:43:56,378
You know,
the villagers also told us

507
00:43:56,475 --> 00:43:58,706
Pankot Palace
had taken something.

508
00:43:58,793 --> 00:44:01,443
Dr. Jones,
in our country,

509
00:44:01,530 --> 00:44:04,661
it's not usual for a guest
to insult his host.

510
00:44:05,826 --> 00:44:06,928
I'm sorry.

511
00:44:07,962 --> 00:44:09,601
I thought we were
talking about folklore.

512
00:44:10,408 --> 00:44:14,302
Excuse me, sir, do you have
anything simple, like soup?

513
00:44:15,695 --> 00:44:18,843
What exactly was it
they say was stolen?

514
00:44:20,175 --> 00:44:21,251
A sacred rock.

515
00:44:22,634 --> 00:44:23,810
[CHATTAR SCOFFS]

516
00:44:24,663 --> 00:44:26,913
You see, Captain,
a rock!

517
00:44:28,301 --> 00:44:30,184
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

518
00:44:33,567 --> 00:44:34,945
[INHALING]

519
00:44:37,789 --> 00:44:39,486
[SCREAMING]

520
00:44:39,573 --> 00:44:42,107
[WHIMPERING]

521
00:44:42,229 --> 00:44:46,240
Something connected
the villagers' rock

522
00:44:46,537 --> 00:44:49,367
and the old legend
of the Sankara Stones.

523
00:44:49,494 --> 00:44:53,853
CHATTAR: Dr. Jones,
we are all vulnerable to vicious rumors.

524
00:44:54,040 --> 00:44:56,259
I seem to
remember that in Honduras

525
00:44:56,356 --> 00:44:58,082
you were accused
of being a grave robber

526
00:44:58,169 --> 00:44:59,714
rather than
an archeologist.

527
00:45:00,291 --> 00:45:03,431
Well, the newspapers
greatly exaggerated the incident.

528
00:45:03,638 --> 00:45:05,590
And wasn't it
the Sultan of Madagascar

529
00:45:05,667 --> 00:45:07,063
who threatened
to cut your head off

530
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:08,384
if you ever returned
to his country?

531
00:45:08,471 --> 00:45:09,479
No, it wasn't my head.

532
00:45:09,566 --> 00:45:10,951
Then your hands, perhaps.

533
00:45:11,038 --> 00:45:12,889
No, it wasn't my hands,

534
00:45:12,986 --> 00:45:14,057
it was my...

535
00:45:15,478 --> 00:45:16,684
My misunderstanding.

536
00:45:16,801 --> 00:45:18,916
Exactly what we have here,
Dr. Jones.

537
00:45:19,223 --> 00:45:22,136
MAHARAJAH: I have heard
the evil stories of the Thuggee cult.

538
00:45:22,223 --> 00:45:23,414
[MUSIC STOPS]

539
00:45:23,501 --> 00:45:26,009
I thought the stories were told
to frighten children.

540
00:45:27,036 --> 00:45:29,979
Later, I learnt
the Thuggee cult was once real

541
00:45:30,296 --> 00:45:32,426
and did of unspeakable things.

542
00:45:33,203 --> 00:45:37,847
I am ashamed of what happened here
so many years ago, and I assure you

543
00:45:37,954 --> 00:45:41,539
this will never happen again
in my kingdom.

544
00:45:43,220 --> 00:45:44,477
If I offended you,

545
00:45:46,407 --> 00:45:47,586
then I am sorry.

546
00:45:47,701 --> 00:45:49,686
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

547
00:45:58,738 --> 00:45:59,861
Dessert!

548
00:46:13,344 --> 00:46:15,720
Chilled monkey brains.

549
00:46:19,455 --> 00:46:21,587
[MOANING]

550
00:46:22,545 --> 00:46:23,568
[THUDDING]

551
00:46:24,370 --> 00:46:25,436
[YAWNS]

552
00:46:31,103 --> 00:46:33,175
I think I'll just
check on Willie.

553
00:46:34,948 --> 00:46:36,210
That's all
you better do.

554
00:46:38,699 --> 00:46:40,540
Tell me later
what happened.

555
00:46:40,867 --> 00:46:41,996
Am-scray.

556
00:46:53,619 --> 00:46:54,963
I've got something for you.

557
00:46:55,720 --> 00:46:59,451
There's nothing you have
that I could possibly want.

558
00:46:59,708 --> 00:47:00,770
Right.

559
00:47:08,634 --> 00:47:10,279
[MOANING]

560
00:47:14,031 --> 00:47:15,640
You're a very nice man.

561
00:47:15,877 --> 00:47:17,716
Maybe you could
be my palace slave.

562
00:47:28,595 --> 00:47:30,299
Wear your jewels
to bed, Princess?

563
00:47:31,570 --> 00:47:32,702
Yeah.

564
00:47:35,008 --> 00:47:36,139
And nothing else.

565
00:47:37,010 --> 00:47:38,185
That shock you?

566
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:39,578
Nothing shocks me.

567
00:47:40,753 --> 00:47:41,856
I'm a scientist.

568
00:47:43,808 --> 00:47:46,380
So, as a scientist,
you do a lot of research?

569
00:47:47,499 --> 00:47:48,595
Always.

570
00:47:49,222 --> 00:47:51,528
And what sort of research
would you do on me?

571
00:47:55,096 --> 00:47:56,554
Nocturnal activities.

572
00:47:56,651 --> 00:47:59,639
You mean like what sort of cream
I put on my face at night,

573
00:47:59,716 --> 00:48:01,557
what position
I like to sleep in?

574
00:48:01,644 --> 00:48:03,036
Mating customs.

575
00:48:03,123 --> 00:48:04,429
Love rituals?

576
00:48:04,516 --> 00:48:07,272
Primitive sexual practices.

577
00:48:07,349 --> 00:48:09,216
So you're an authority
in that area?

578
00:48:09,303 --> 00:48:10,794
Years of fieldwork.

579
00:48:20,030 --> 00:48:22,573
I don't blame you
for being sore at me.

580
00:48:23,110 --> 00:48:24,665
I can be
hard to handle.

581
00:48:26,495 --> 00:48:27,639
I've had worse.

582
00:48:29,066 --> 00:48:30,673
But you'll never
have better.

583
00:48:33,947 --> 00:48:35,100
I don't know.

584
00:48:35,777 --> 00:48:38,129
As a scientist, I don't want
to prejudice my experiment.

585
00:48:38,227 --> 00:48:39,464
I'll let you know
in the morning.

586
00:48:40,944 --> 00:48:43,468
Why, you conceited ape.

587
00:48:43,555 --> 00:48:45,470
I'm not that easy.

588
00:48:47,559 --> 00:48:49,169
I'm not that easy, either.

589
00:48:49,987 --> 00:48:51,648
Trouble with you is, Willie,

590
00:48:51,755 --> 00:48:53,609
you're too used to
getting your own way.

591
00:48:54,818 --> 00:48:56,108
And you're just
too proud to admit

592
00:48:56,215 --> 00:48:58,791
that you're crazy
about me, Dr. Jones.

593
00:48:59,948 --> 00:49:02,677
If you want me, Willie,
you know where you can find me.

594
00:49:03,314 --> 00:49:04,579
Five minutes.

595
00:49:04,916 --> 00:49:06,827
You'll be back over here
in five minutes.

596
00:49:06,934 --> 00:49:08,537
I'll be asleep
in five minutes.

597
00:49:08,624 --> 00:49:09,876
Five.

598
00:49:10,003 --> 00:49:11,931
You know it, and I know it.

599
00:49:26,990 --> 00:49:28,914
Five minutes.

600
00:49:31,211 --> 00:49:32,488
Four and a half.

601
00:49:48,955 --> 00:49:49,965
[SNIFFING]

602
00:50:02,980 --> 00:50:07,085
[CLOCK TICKING]

603
00:50:22,653 --> 00:50:24,220
[GASPS]

604
00:50:27,049 --> 00:50:28,299
[CHUCKLES] "Palace slave."

605
00:50:29,617 --> 00:50:32,038
"Nocturnal activities."

606
00:50:33,471 --> 00:50:35,683
I'm a "conceited ape"?
[SCOFFS]

607
00:50:35,875 --> 00:50:37,682
"I'll tell you
in the morning."

608
00:50:39,583 --> 00:50:40,715
I can't believe it.

609
00:50:41,454 --> 00:50:42,725
He's not coming.

610
00:50:43,202 --> 00:50:44,317
She's not coming.

611
00:50:47,170 --> 00:50:48,404
I can't believe
I'm not going.

612
00:50:48,461 --> 00:50:49,585
[GRUNTS]

613
00:50:51,551 --> 00:50:53,426
[GRUNTING]

614
00:51:08,830 --> 00:51:10,359
Indiana Jones!

615
00:51:10,476 --> 00:51:13,012
This is one night
you'll never forget!

616
00:51:13,079 --> 00:51:16,857
This is the night I slipped right
through your fingers!

617
00:51:18,381 --> 00:51:19,561
Sleep tight,

618
00:51:19,708 --> 00:51:21,298
and pleasant dreams!

619
00:51:21,385 --> 00:51:22,788
[CHOKING]

620
00:51:24,540 --> 00:51:27,054
I could have been
your greatest adventure.

621
00:51:30,760 --> 00:51:31,817
[CRASHING]

622
00:51:31,884 --> 00:51:33,081
[GASPS]

623
00:51:37,728 --> 00:51:39,138
Dr. Jones, your whip!

624
00:51:47,477 --> 00:51:48,557
[GROANS]

625
00:52:00,309 --> 00:52:01,447
Shorty,

626
00:52:01,534 --> 00:52:02,571
turn off the switch.

627
00:52:08,774 --> 00:52:10,238
Oh, Indy.

628
00:52:11,588 --> 00:52:12,676
Be gentle with me.

629
00:52:12,763 --> 00:52:14,069
Be gentle with me.

630
00:52:20,292 --> 00:52:21,529
But I'm here.

631
00:52:34,002 --> 00:52:35,114
There's nobody here.

632
00:52:35,211 --> 00:52:37,005
No, I'm here.

633
00:52:38,385 --> 00:52:41,248
Indy, you're acting
awfully strange.

634
00:53:07,009 --> 00:53:09,146
Hey, I'm right here.

635
00:53:10,690 --> 00:53:11,821
[SCREAMS]

636
00:53:22,157 --> 00:53:26,453
"Follow in
the footsteps of Siva."

637
00:53:26,600 --> 00:53:27,779
WILLIE: What does that mean?

638
00:53:31,481 --> 00:53:34,375
"Do not betray
these truths."

639
00:53:34,792 --> 00:53:37,065
Shorty, go get our stuff.

640
00:53:38,427 --> 00:53:39,518
[WILLIE MOANS]

641
00:54:06,433 --> 00:54:07,916
INDY: Stay behind me,
Short Round.

642
00:54:09,504 --> 00:54:13,760
Step where I step,
and don't touch anything.

643
00:54:19,716 --> 00:54:21,004
[SHORTY SCREAMS]

644
00:54:22,153 --> 00:54:25,615
[PANTING HEAVILY]

645
00:54:25,722 --> 00:54:26,942
I step where you step.

646
00:54:27,169 --> 00:54:28,855
I touch nothing.

647
00:54:30,465 --> 00:54:32,075
Indy!

648
00:54:51,272 --> 00:54:53,098
[CRUNCHING]

649
00:54:53,205 --> 00:54:54,576
SHORTY:
I step on something.

650
00:54:56,004 --> 00:54:58,283
INDY: Yeah, there's something
on the ground.

651
00:54:58,410 --> 00:55:00,184
Feel like step
on fortune cookies.

652
00:55:01,945 --> 00:55:03,641
It's not
fortune cookies.

653
00:55:06,240 --> 00:55:07,437
Let me take a look.

654
00:55:11,926 --> 00:55:14,558
[RATTLING]

655
00:55:18,774 --> 00:55:20,265
[SCREECHING]

656
00:55:21,711 --> 00:55:24,126
[PANTING]
That's no cookies.

657
00:55:24,221 --> 00:55:25,476
INDY: It's all right.
I got him.

658
00:55:29,176 --> 00:55:30,786
Go. There, go.

659
00:55:39,708 --> 00:55:40,854
[RUMBLING]

660
00:56:11,110 --> 00:56:12,219
Stop.

661
00:56:12,326 --> 00:56:15,465
Look, just stand
up against the wall, will you?

662
00:56:22,388 --> 00:56:25,172
[RUMBLING]

663
00:56:26,233 --> 00:56:27,295
[GASPS]

664
00:56:27,402 --> 00:56:30,632
[RUMBLING CONTINUES]

665
00:56:30,706 --> 00:56:32,761
You say to stand
against the wall!

666
00:56:32,848 --> 00:56:34,197
I listen to what you say!

667
00:56:34,284 --> 00:56:36,199
- Not my fault! Not my fault!
- Willie, get down here!

668
00:56:36,286 --> 00:56:37,615
We're in trouble!

669
00:56:38,352 --> 00:56:41,172
Willie! Willie!

670
00:56:41,269 --> 00:56:43,882
Bet I get
all dirty again.

671
00:56:44,149 --> 00:56:45,861
Willie, get down here! Not my fault!

672
00:56:45,948 --> 00:56:47,266
We're in trouble!

673
00:56:47,393 --> 00:56:50,344
Trouble? Trouble?
What sort of...

674
00:56:50,431 --> 00:56:53,237
[SCREAMING]

675
00:57:05,794 --> 00:57:07,477
This is serious!

676
00:57:07,614 --> 00:57:11,117
There are two dead
people down here!

677
00:57:11,184 --> 00:57:14,375
There're going to be
two dead people in here! Hurry!

678
00:57:14,482 --> 00:57:16,649
I've almost had
enough of you two.

679
00:57:16,761 --> 00:57:17,893
Willie!

680
00:57:17,980 --> 00:57:19,477
What's the rush?

681
00:57:19,934 --> 00:57:22,870
It's a long story, Willie.
Hurry, or you don't get to hear it.

682
00:57:24,974 --> 00:57:27,877
God, what is this?

683
00:57:29,631 --> 00:57:31,388
Indy, what is this?

684
00:57:31,465 --> 00:57:33,560
I can't see a thing!

685
00:57:34,301 --> 00:57:35,519
Hurry!

686
00:57:35,606 --> 00:57:36,757
All right!

687
00:57:37,274 --> 00:57:39,829
Oh, I broke a nail.

688
00:57:47,878 --> 00:57:50,056
[RATTLING]

689
00:57:51,589 --> 00:57:53,233
[SCREAMING]

690
00:57:53,320 --> 00:57:55,104
Willie, hurry!

691
00:57:55,191 --> 00:57:56,435
WILLIE: They're in my hair!

692
00:57:56,543 --> 00:57:58,499
INDY: Shut up, Willie!

693
00:58:00,109 --> 00:58:01,415
Indy, let me in!

694
00:58:01,502 --> 00:58:02,633
SHORTY: No, let us out!

695
00:58:02,720 --> 00:58:03,724
Let me in!

696
00:58:03,821 --> 00:58:04,924
Let us out!

697
00:58:04,991 --> 00:58:06,594
INDY: Shut up!
- I'm down here!

698
00:58:06,681 --> 00:58:08,209
They're all over me!

699
00:58:08,956 --> 00:58:11,381
There's got to be a fulcrum release
lever somewhere.

700
00:58:11,468 --> 00:58:12,487
What?

701
00:58:12,564 --> 00:58:14,554
A handle that
opens the door.

702
00:58:14,681 --> 00:58:16,374
Go on! They're just,
just square holes!

703
00:58:16,461 --> 00:58:17,895
INDY: Go to
the right hole.

704
00:58:19,389 --> 00:58:20,454
SHORTY: Hurry, Willie!

705
00:58:22,203 --> 00:58:23,620
[GROANING IN DISGUST]

706
00:58:25,439 --> 00:58:27,655
[SCREAMING]

707
00:58:27,772 --> 00:58:30,558
INDY: The other one!
The other right. Your other right!

708
00:58:30,625 --> 00:58:33,311
- The one on your right!
- There's slime inside!

709
00:58:33,664 --> 00:58:34,856
I can't do it.

710
00:58:35,623 --> 00:58:37,451
You can do it. Feel inside.

711
00:58:38,178 --> 00:58:39,225
Okay.

712
00:58:39,844 --> 00:58:41,529
[RATTLING]

713
00:58:42,195 --> 00:58:43,845
You feel inside!

714
00:58:43,935 --> 00:58:45,241
Do it now!

715
00:58:45,328 --> 00:58:46,416
Okay!

716
00:58:47,765 --> 00:58:50,058
[RUMBLING]

717
00:58:56,009 --> 00:59:00,659
Willie, we are going to die!

718
00:59:01,910 --> 00:59:03,254
WILLIE: It's soft.

719
00:59:06,219 --> 00:59:07,593
It's moving!

720
00:59:07,689 --> 00:59:10,449
[RATTLING]

721
00:59:15,809 --> 00:59:16,916
Got it!

722
00:59:31,551 --> 00:59:33,627
Get 'em off of me!
Get 'em off of me!

723
00:59:33,704 --> 00:59:35,489
They're all over me!
Get 'em off me!

724
00:59:38,772 --> 00:59:39,860
No!

725
00:59:42,384 --> 00:59:44,137
It wasn't me! It's her!

726
00:59:44,224 --> 00:59:45,248
Huh?

727
00:59:46,127 --> 00:59:47,427
Come on!

728
00:59:47,504 --> 00:59:50,632
Go! Move! Come on,
move! Come on!

729
01:00:20,126 --> 01:00:22,076
[CHANTING]

730
01:00:44,761 --> 01:00:46,056
[DRUM BEATING]

731
01:00:46,784 --> 01:00:51,546
[CHANTING CONTINUES]

732
01:00:51,671 --> 01:00:53,306
It's a Thuggee ceremony.

733
01:00:53,563 --> 01:00:55,074
They're worshipping Kali.

734
01:01:04,949 --> 01:01:07,011
Have you ever seen
anything like this before?

735
01:01:07,508 --> 01:01:09,601
Nobody's seen this
for a hundred years.

736
01:01:32,069 --> 01:01:36,710
[CHANTING]

737
01:01:51,110 --> 01:01:56,582
[MAN SPEAKING HINDI]

738
01:02:07,994 --> 01:02:10,967
[MAN CHANTING]

739
01:02:32,043 --> 01:02:37,550
[SPEAKING HINDI]

740
01:02:44,827 --> 01:02:49,716
Kali Ma. Kali Ma...

741
01:02:50,398 --> 01:02:51,702
Kali Ma!

742
01:02:53,069 --> 01:02:58,058
[HEART BEATING]

743
01:03:03,915 --> 01:03:08,231
[SCREAMING]

744
01:03:11,246 --> 01:03:12,922
- [SCREAMING]
- [GASPS]

745
01:03:13,021 --> 01:03:17,861
[MOLA SPEAKING IN HINDI]

746
01:03:17,952 --> 01:03:20,210
[ALL CHEERING]

747
01:03:28,741 --> 01:03:30,133
He's still alive.

748
01:03:30,220 --> 01:03:33,356
[CHANTING]

749
01:03:33,457 --> 01:03:36,212
[GASPING]

750
01:04:06,221 --> 01:04:07,780
[SCREAMING]

751
01:04:36,364 --> 01:04:38,680
[LAUGHING MANIACALLY]

752
01:04:54,913 --> 01:04:56,349
Kali Ma.

753
01:05:24,646 --> 01:05:29,278
[CHEERING]

754
01:05:58,062 --> 01:06:00,144
That's the rock they took
from the village.

755
01:06:01,381 --> 01:06:03,503
It's one of
the Sankara Stones.

756
01:06:11,043 --> 01:06:13,208
- Why they glow like that?
- [SHUSHING]

757
01:06:14,993 --> 01:06:16,328
The legend says

758
01:06:16,535 --> 01:06:18,013
when the rocks are
brought together,

759
01:06:18,110 --> 01:06:20,041
the diamonds
inside them will glow.

760
01:06:20,999 --> 01:06:22,130
Diamonds?

761
01:06:22,217 --> 01:06:23,392
Diamonds.

762
01:06:23,479 --> 01:06:24,480
- Diamonds!
- Shh!

763
01:06:24,568 --> 01:06:25,611
Diamonds.

764
01:06:42,716 --> 01:06:43,906
Hey, hey.

765
01:06:44,063 --> 01:06:48,113
Look, I want you two
to stay up here and keep quiet.

766
01:06:48,200 --> 01:06:49,337
Shorty,
you keep an eye on her.

767
01:06:49,424 --> 01:06:51,126
- Why, where are you going?
- Down there.

768
01:06:51,243 --> 01:06:53,529
Down there? Are you crazy?

769
01:06:54,446 --> 01:06:57,536
I'm not leaving here
without the stones.

770
01:06:57,653 --> 01:07:00,301
You could get killed chasing after
your damn fortune and glory!

771
01:07:00,778 --> 01:07:01,791
Maybe.

772
01:07:03,389 --> 01:07:04,673
But not today.

773
01:08:20,684 --> 01:08:22,033
[MOUTHING] Be careful.

774
01:08:55,936 --> 01:08:57,938
[SCREAMING IN DISTANCE]

775
01:09:32,276 --> 01:09:33,472
Where's he going?

776
01:09:34,844 --> 01:09:36,454
[SCREAMING]

777
01:09:36,541 --> 01:09:37,925
Let me go!

778
01:09:40,986 --> 01:09:43,987
Run, Willie! Run!

779
01:10:14,231 --> 01:10:17,375
[SPEAKING HINDI]

780
01:10:19,758 --> 01:10:22,035
[GROWLING]

781
01:10:34,158 --> 01:10:36,644
[SPEAKING HINDI]

782
01:11:17,769 --> 01:11:18,991
Dr. Jones!

783
01:11:21,689 --> 01:11:23,087
I keep telling you,

784
01:11:23,184 --> 01:11:25,496
you listen me more,
you live longer.

785
01:11:26,253 --> 01:11:28,441
BOY: Please, let me die.

786
01:11:30,394 --> 01:11:31,921
I pray to Siva,

787
01:11:32,150 --> 01:11:35,090
"Let me die,"
but I do not.

788
01:11:35,967 --> 01:11:38,879
Now...
Now the evil of Kali take me.

789
01:11:40,510 --> 01:11:41,514
How?

790
01:11:41,621 --> 01:11:44,261
They will make me drink
the blood of the Kali.

791
01:11:44,678 --> 01:11:47,891
Then I'll fall into
the Black Sleep of the Kali Ma.

792
01:11:48,238 --> 01:11:49,325
What is that?

793
01:11:50,508 --> 01:11:51,962
We become like them.

794
01:11:54,372 --> 01:11:57,671
We'll be alive,
but like a nightmare.

795
01:11:58,268 --> 01:12:01,745
You drink blood, you not wake up
from nightmare.

796
01:12:13,700 --> 01:12:17,550
You were caught trying to steal
the Sankara Stones.

797
01:12:18,383 --> 01:12:20,357
There were five stones
in the beginning.

798
01:12:21,394 --> 01:12:24,258
Over the centuries,
they were dispersed by wars,

799
01:12:24,355 --> 01:12:26,667
sold off by thieves
like you.

800
01:12:26,754 --> 01:12:28,060
Thieves like me, huh?

801
01:12:28,147 --> 01:12:29,181
[SCOFFS]

802
01:12:30,062 --> 01:12:31,627
Still missing two.

803
01:12:33,094 --> 01:12:35,353
A century ago, when the British
raided this temple

804
01:12:35,450 --> 01:12:36,866
and butchered
my people,

805
01:12:37,423 --> 01:12:41,592
a loyal priest hid the last two stones
down here in the catacombs.

806
01:12:41,729 --> 01:12:44,729
So that's what you've got these slaves
digging for, huh?

807
01:12:45,590 --> 01:12:46,964
They're innocent children.

808
01:12:47,081 --> 01:12:49,849
They dig for the gems
to support our cause.

809
01:12:51,315 --> 01:12:53,564
They also search
for the last two stones.

810
01:12:56,312 --> 01:12:59,507
Soon we will have
all the five Sankara Stones,

811
01:12:59,974 --> 01:13:02,213
and the Thuggees
will be all powerful.

812
01:13:03,574 --> 01:13:06,142
What a vivid imagination.

813
01:13:06,229 --> 01:13:07,404
[MOLA LAUGHING]

814
01:13:11,124 --> 01:13:14,206
You don't believe me?

815
01:13:15,597 --> 01:13:18,109
You will, Dr. Jones.

816
01:13:20,421 --> 01:13:24,725
You will become
a true believer.

817
01:13:24,812 --> 01:13:29,464
[BOTH LAUGHING]

818
01:13:29,567 --> 01:13:32,280
[GATE CREAKING]

819
01:13:42,020 --> 01:13:43,092
Hi.

820
01:14:01,500 --> 01:14:08,156
[SPEAKING HINDI]

821
01:14:08,255 --> 01:14:09,291
SHORTY: Dr. Jones!

822
01:14:09,378 --> 01:14:10,727
Don't drink, it's bad!

823
01:14:10,814 --> 01:14:11,949
Don't drink!

824
01:14:12,816 --> 01:14:13,991
Spit it out!

825
01:14:17,641 --> 01:14:20,266
[SPEAKING HINDI]

826
01:14:39,930 --> 01:14:41,208
[GROANING]

827
01:14:43,803 --> 01:14:45,718
[GROANING]

828
01:14:48,304 --> 01:14:50,462
Dr. Jones...
[SPEAKING CHINESE]

829
01:14:52,006 --> 01:14:54,452
[SPEAKING HINDI]

830
01:15:01,169 --> 01:15:03,783
[SHOUTING IN CHINESE]

831
01:15:07,875 --> 01:15:11,412
You dare not do that.

832
01:15:16,271 --> 01:15:19,313
[SPEAKING HINDI]

833
01:15:27,847 --> 01:15:29,087
[SCREAMS]

834
01:15:29,817 --> 01:15:31,853
Leave him alone,
you bastards!

835
01:15:42,549 --> 01:15:44,716
The British in India
will be slaughtered.

836
01:15:44,843 --> 01:15:46,838
Then we will
overrun the Muslims.

837
01:15:47,035 --> 01:15:49,212
Then the Hebrew God
will fall.

838
01:15:50,709 --> 01:15:53,438
And then the Christian God
will be cast down and forgotten.

839
01:15:53,525 --> 01:15:54,629
[CHOKING]

840
01:15:56,175 --> 01:15:59,211
Soon, Kali Ma
will rule the world.

841
01:16:00,358 --> 01:16:01,755
[COUGHING]

842
01:16:05,624 --> 01:16:07,401
Dr. Jones...

843
01:16:20,291 --> 01:16:22,880
[GASPING]

844
01:16:25,470 --> 01:16:26,950
[GROANING LOUDLY]

845
01:16:27,037 --> 01:16:28,271
[ECHOING]

846
01:17:04,640 --> 01:17:08,079
[LAUGHING]

847
01:17:10,515 --> 01:17:12,387
[CROWS CAWING]

848
01:17:17,435 --> 01:17:18,770
[SPEAKS HINDI]

849
01:17:23,572 --> 01:17:25,325
[SPEAKS HINDI]

850
01:17:40,753 --> 01:17:43,358
[SPEAKING HINDI]

851
01:17:51,034 --> 01:17:53,106
Kali Ma protects us.

852
01:17:53,993 --> 01:17:55,734
We are her children.

853
01:17:57,222 --> 01:17:59,608
We pledge our devotion to her

854
01:17:59,695 --> 01:18:01,610
with an offering of flesh...

855
01:18:01,697 --> 01:18:02,959
WILLIE:
What are you doing?

856
01:18:06,179 --> 01:18:07,557
...and blood.

857
01:18:17,453 --> 01:18:21,675
Your friend has seen,
and she has heard.

858
01:18:22,892 --> 01:18:25,663
Now she will not talk.

859
01:18:35,257 --> 01:18:36,866
I'm not going to have
anything nice to say

860
01:18:36,943 --> 01:18:38,730
about this place
when I get back.

861
01:18:39,197 --> 01:18:42,564
Indy! For God sakes,
help me!

862
01:18:42,651 --> 01:18:44,870
What's the matter with you?

863
01:18:44,957 --> 01:18:46,037
[WILLIE SOBBING]

864
01:18:47,917 --> 01:18:49,266
[MEN CHANTING]

865
01:18:59,754 --> 01:19:02,278
No, no.

866
01:19:02,965 --> 01:19:05,934
[SPEAKING HINDI]

867
01:19:33,570 --> 01:19:34,789
MOLA: Come.

868
01:19:37,661 --> 01:19:38,880
Come.

869
01:20:01,685 --> 01:20:03,135
Indiana...

870
01:20:05,123 --> 01:20:08,660
Indiana, help us.

871
01:20:22,358 --> 01:20:24,229
Please, snap out of it.

872
01:20:25,931 --> 01:20:27,972
[SOBBING]
You're not one of them.

873
01:20:30,453 --> 01:20:32,007
You're not one of them.

874
01:20:35,719 --> 01:20:37,373
Please come back to us.

875
01:20:38,505 --> 01:20:39,842
Don't leave me.

876
01:20:52,649 --> 01:20:56,245
- [CHANTING IN HINDI]
- [SCREAMING] No!

877
01:20:58,753 --> 01:21:00,212
What are you doing?

878
01:21:01,049 --> 01:21:02,442
Are you mad?

879
01:21:03,791 --> 01:21:06,072
[CHANTING IN HINDI]

880
01:21:09,485 --> 01:21:11,146
[SPITS]

881
01:21:20,875 --> 01:21:23,467
[CONTINUES CHANTING]

882
01:21:36,196 --> 01:21:39,038
[ALL SHOUTING]

883
01:21:40,349 --> 01:21:42,351
[SHOUTING IN HINDI]

884
01:22:19,448 --> 01:22:21,918
This can't be happening,
this can't be happening.

885
01:22:22,710 --> 01:22:25,971
Wake up, Willie, wake up.

886
01:22:40,975 --> 01:22:45,173
[SCREAMING]

887
01:22:56,947 --> 01:23:00,341
No! No! No!

888
01:23:11,832 --> 01:23:13,918
No, no, no!

889
01:23:14,444 --> 01:23:16,445
Wake up, Dr. Jones,
wake up!

890
01:23:20,928 --> 01:23:22,451
Dr. Jones!

891
01:23:23,408 --> 01:23:24,862
[COMMANDS IN HINDI]

892
01:23:30,677 --> 01:23:32,445
[GROANING]

893
01:23:38,336 --> 01:23:40,291
Indy, I love you.

894
01:23:41,159 --> 01:23:44,215
- Wake up, Indy! Wake up!
- [SCREAMS]

895
01:23:46,007 --> 01:23:48,781
You're my best friend!
Wake up, Indy!

896
01:23:54,308 --> 01:23:56,049
Wait! Wait!

897
01:23:56,913 --> 01:23:58,486
He's mine!

898
01:24:02,359 --> 01:24:03,641
I'm all right, kid.

899
01:24:11,196 --> 01:24:14,682
[ALL CLAMORING]

900
01:24:49,461 --> 01:24:50,639
Mola Ram!

901
01:24:50,703 --> 01:24:53,079
[LAUGHING MANIACALLY]

902
01:25:25,268 --> 01:25:27,423
[GRUNTING]

903
01:25:32,101 --> 01:25:33,886
[CHATTAR LAUGHING]

904
01:25:47,421 --> 01:25:48,926
[MOANING]

905
01:26:06,919 --> 01:26:08,814
[ALL CLAMORING]

906
01:26:12,402 --> 01:26:13,882
Give me some slack!

907
01:26:29,985 --> 01:26:31,099
[WILLIE MOANS]

908
01:26:33,353 --> 01:26:35,730
Willie, Willie, wake up!

909
01:26:38,145 --> 01:26:40,706
Willie, Willie, it's me!
I'm back!

910
01:26:43,346 --> 01:26:44,613
Oh, Indy.

911
01:27:13,028 --> 01:27:14,813
Indy, my friend.

912
01:27:16,292 --> 01:27:17,903
I'm sorry, kid.

913
01:27:25,094 --> 01:27:27,911
Indy, now,
let's get out of here.

914
01:27:30,654 --> 01:27:33,093
Right. All of us.

915
01:27:35,771 --> 01:27:37,751
[SPEAKING HINDI]

916
01:27:56,475 --> 01:27:57,768
[ALL SHOUTING]

917
01:28:10,914 --> 01:28:14,200
[CHILDREN CLAMORING]

918
01:28:46,512 --> 01:28:47,861
WILLIE: No!

919
01:29:04,754 --> 01:29:05,966
I've got to save him!

920
01:29:06,053 --> 01:29:07,054
He can take care of himself.

921
01:29:07,141 --> 01:29:08,161
He needs me.

922
01:29:08,763 --> 01:29:10,870
[MOANS]

923
01:29:10,965 --> 01:29:12,174
I've got to save Indy!

924
01:29:24,463 --> 01:29:26,092
Okay, save him.

925
01:29:30,556 --> 01:29:31,656
Drop him down!

926
01:29:31,943 --> 01:29:33,907
I kill you!
Drop him down!

927
01:30:01,326 --> 01:30:03,698
[MOANING]

928
01:30:05,514 --> 01:30:07,192
What's the matter with him?

929
01:30:09,725 --> 01:30:11,186
[MOANING]

930
01:30:50,375 --> 01:30:52,116
Here. Try this.

931
01:31:22,667 --> 01:31:24,586
[SCREAMING]

932
01:31:37,857 --> 01:31:39,630
[LAUGHS]

933
01:31:57,355 --> 01:31:58,903
[SCREAMING]

934
01:32:07,834 --> 01:32:09,238
Go, Indy!

935
01:32:34,346 --> 01:32:36,817
[SCREAMING]

936
01:32:38,918 --> 01:32:41,754
[PLEADING IN HINDI]

937
01:32:55,108 --> 01:32:56,395
[EXCLAIMS IN DISGUST]

938
01:32:57,676 --> 01:32:58,829
[SCREAMS]

939
01:33:05,031 --> 01:33:06,911
[SCREAMS]

940
01:33:11,369 --> 01:33:13,024
It was
the Black Sleep of Kali.

941
01:33:27,119 --> 01:33:28,293
Short Round!

942
01:33:29,302 --> 01:33:32,420
Quit fooling around with that kid!
Get down in the cart, now!

943
01:33:32,927 --> 01:33:34,478
Okeydokey, Indy!

944
01:33:34,565 --> 01:33:37,545
Please listen. To get out, you must
take the left tunnel.

945
01:33:37,671 --> 01:33:38,803
Thank you.

946
01:33:49,562 --> 01:33:50,865
[SCREAMS]

947
01:34:27,025 --> 01:34:28,592
Shorty! Quit stalling!

948
01:34:28,649 --> 01:34:29,810
[COMMANDING IN HINDI]

949
01:34:29,897 --> 01:34:30,931
SHORTY: Come on, Indy!

950
01:34:30,988 --> 01:34:32,204
Go!

951
01:34:32,291 --> 01:34:33,538
Go! Go!

952
01:34:36,915 --> 01:34:38,515
Shorty, look out!

953
01:34:46,215 --> 01:34:47,219
Come on!

954
01:34:47,306 --> 01:34:48,333
Indy!

955
01:34:53,747 --> 01:34:55,061
Hurry!

956
01:35:00,145 --> 01:35:02,345
Hurry! Hurry up!

957
01:35:05,106 --> 01:35:07,609
[ORDERING IN HINDI]

958
01:35:07,716 --> 01:35:11,284
SHORTY: Indy, take the left tunnel!
The left tunnel!

959
01:35:11,381 --> 01:35:14,183
No, Indy!
You missed it! Left tunnel!

960
01:35:41,795 --> 01:35:43,579
[GUNSHOTS]

961
01:35:44,972 --> 01:35:46,322
We got company!

962
01:35:51,022 --> 01:35:52,293
Stop. Let her go!

963
01:35:52,750 --> 01:35:54,895
- Let go of the brake.
- What?

964
01:35:54,982 --> 01:35:56,433
- What?
- Let her go.

965
01:35:56,510 --> 01:35:58,034
Our only chance
is to outrun them.

966
01:36:15,133 --> 01:36:16,178
Shorty? Huh?

967
01:36:16,285 --> 01:36:17,625
Come up here and
take the brake.

968
01:36:19,374 --> 01:36:21,966
Watch it on the curves,
or we'll fly right off the track.

969
01:36:22,053 --> 01:36:23,113
SHORTY: Okay.

970
01:37:05,096 --> 01:37:06,309
[SCREAMING]

971
01:37:19,153 --> 01:37:20,828
[CHEERING]

972
01:37:22,635 --> 01:37:23,636
[GUNSHOTS]

973
01:37:29,168 --> 01:37:32,099
[ORDERING IN HINDI]

974
01:37:44,744 --> 01:37:45,888
What are you doing?

975
01:37:45,985 --> 01:37:47,051
Short cut.

976
01:37:47,138 --> 01:37:48,552
- Yes, Indy.
- Short, cut.

977
01:38:12,685 --> 01:38:13,744
INDY: Watch it.

978
01:38:18,430 --> 01:38:19,935
SHORTY: Indy, help!

979
01:38:22,697 --> 01:38:24,854
WILLIE: Hang on!
- Indy!

980
01:38:25,072 --> 01:38:26,074
WILLIE: Pull him in.

981
01:38:26,161 --> 01:38:27,904
SHORTY: Let me go! Let me go!

982
01:38:28,755 --> 01:38:30,310
Let go of him!

983
01:38:31,616 --> 01:38:34,053
SHORTY: No! No!

984
01:38:34,140 --> 01:38:35,228
WILLIE: Pull him in!

985
01:38:35,315 --> 01:38:36,698
- I'll catch him!
- No!

986
01:39:11,743 --> 01:39:12,967
[SCREAMS]

987
01:39:21,274 --> 01:39:23,866
- [SCREAMING]
- Duck!

988
01:39:43,983 --> 01:39:45,081
INDY: All right.
SHORTY: What?

989
01:39:45,168 --> 01:39:46,699
INDY: Brakes. Brakes.

990
01:39:46,806 --> 01:39:48,388
Slow us down.
SHORTY: Okay.

991
01:39:54,074 --> 01:39:56,527
Big mistake.
Big mistake, Indy.

992
01:39:56,614 --> 01:39:57,660
WILLIE: Figures.

993
01:40:18,984 --> 01:40:20,377
We're going too fast!

994
01:40:20,464 --> 01:40:21,804
Too fast!

995
01:40:21,901 --> 01:40:23,351
We're going to crash!

996
01:40:28,250 --> 01:40:29,744
[SCREAMS]

997
01:40:31,257 --> 01:40:33,612
[PANTING]

998
01:40:35,958 --> 01:40:39,309
- Water, water, water!
WILLIE: Look! Look there!Water!

999
01:40:39,396 --> 01:40:41,441
WILLIE: Fire! You're on fire!
- Water, water!

1000
01:40:41,528 --> 01:40:43,626
- Look...
- Water, water.

1001
01:40:45,663 --> 01:40:47,406
Water, water.

1002
01:40:48,187 --> 01:40:50,275
Come on. Come on!

1003
01:41:03,855 --> 01:41:04,943
Let's go!

1004
01:41:09,426 --> 01:41:10,860
Run, run!

1005
01:41:10,957 --> 01:41:12,255
[SCREAMING]

1006
01:41:24,006 --> 01:41:25,510
SHORTY: Willie, look out!

1007
01:41:35,234 --> 01:41:36,627
No!

1008
01:41:36,714 --> 01:41:38,701
Head for the bridge. Go!

1009
01:41:40,606 --> 01:41:42,419
SHORTY: Come on, Willie.
This way.

1010
01:41:55,559 --> 01:41:56,829
WILLIE: Oh, God!

1011
01:41:56,946 --> 01:41:59,071
Come on, let's go.
Strong bridge.

1012
01:41:59,158 --> 01:42:02,087
Come on, let's go.
Strong bridge.

1013
01:42:02,174 --> 01:42:03,654
Look, strong wood.

1014
01:42:04,829 --> 01:42:06,091
Come on!

1015
01:42:06,178 --> 01:42:07,224
Look!

1016
01:42:07,702 --> 01:42:09,094
WILLIE: Shorty!

1017
01:42:11,790 --> 01:42:13,917
Help! I'm falling down.

1018
01:42:16,536 --> 01:42:17,799
Help!

1019
01:42:19,975 --> 01:42:21,098
Not very funny.

1020
01:42:46,529 --> 01:42:47,560
Back!

1021
01:42:49,952 --> 01:42:51,032
[EXCLAIMING]

1022
01:42:53,095 --> 01:42:57,471
[CLAMORING]

1023
01:43:07,149 --> 01:43:10,477
[SCREAMING]

1024
01:43:13,553 --> 01:43:14,986
Welcome.

1025
01:43:16,553 --> 01:43:19,560
[SPEAKS HINDI]

1026
01:43:25,430 --> 01:43:26,834
[MOANS]

1027
01:43:27,911 --> 01:43:29,615
Let her go, Mola Ram.

1028
01:43:29,952 --> 01:43:33,743
You are in a position
unsuitable to give orders.

1029
01:43:34,526 --> 01:43:35,877
Watch your back!

1030
01:43:45,026 --> 01:43:46,831
You want the stones,
let 'em go.

1031
01:43:51,392 --> 01:43:52,654
Let her go!

1032
01:43:52,771 --> 01:43:56,250
[LAUGHING] Drop them,
Dr. Jones.

1033
01:43:57,027 --> 01:43:58,480
They will be found.

1034
01:43:59,377 --> 01:44:00,814
You won't.

1035
01:44:02,685 --> 01:44:04,208
[SHOUTS]

1036
01:44:04,295 --> 01:44:06,925
- Indy!
- Behind you!

1037
01:44:15,611 --> 01:44:17,149
Oh, shit.

1038
01:44:28,432 --> 01:44:29,668
Go on.

1039
01:44:31,018 --> 01:44:32,236
Go.

1040
01:44:41,767 --> 01:44:43,117
MOLA: Go on! Go on!

1041
01:44:44,466 --> 01:44:45,673
Get moving.

1042
01:44:50,080 --> 01:44:51,363
Shorty...

1043
01:44:52,320 --> 01:44:54,869
[SPEAKING CHINESE]

1044
01:44:57,471 --> 01:44:59,593
Hang on, lady.
We going for a ride.

1045
01:45:02,092 --> 01:45:04,288
Oh, my God!

1046
01:45:05,670 --> 01:45:09,558
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

1047
01:45:09,664 --> 01:45:11,514
Is he nuts?

1048
01:45:12,153 --> 01:45:13,495
He no nuts.

1049
01:45:13,582 --> 01:45:15,291
He's crazy.

1050
01:45:15,358 --> 01:45:19,581
Mola Ram, prepare to meet Kali

1051
01:45:20,328 --> 01:45:21,851
in hell.

1052
01:45:23,124 --> 01:45:24,227
What are you doing?

1053
01:45:24,645 --> 01:45:26,542
[SCREAMING] You fool!

1054
01:46:13,859 --> 01:46:16,168
[MOLA SPEAKING HINDI]

1055
01:46:26,518 --> 01:46:28,265
Indy, cover your heart!

1056
01:46:28,352 --> 01:46:29,573
Cover your heart!

1057
01:46:30,964 --> 01:46:32,617
Oh, my God!

1058
01:46:32,704 --> 01:46:37,453
[MOLA CHANTING]

1059
01:46:42,497 --> 01:46:43,585
Oh, my God.

1060
01:47:05,911 --> 01:47:08,036
[BOTH SPEAKING HINDI]

1061
01:47:22,928 --> 01:47:25,901
[ORDERING IN HINDI]

1062
01:47:26,830 --> 01:47:28,553
- Look out!
- No!

1063
01:47:38,727 --> 01:47:40,055
[YELLING]

1064
01:47:43,654 --> 01:47:46,412
[GROANING]

1065
01:47:53,771 --> 01:47:55,454
No!

1066
01:47:59,878 --> 01:48:01,097
SHORTY: Come on. Let's go!

1067
01:48:02,446 --> 01:48:04,217
The stones are mine!

1068
01:48:05,390 --> 01:48:07,210
You've betrayed Siva.

1069
01:48:08,397 --> 01:48:11,628
[SPEAKING HINDI]

1070
01:48:11,715 --> 01:48:13,104
You betrayed Siva.

1071
01:48:14,642 --> 01:48:17,319
[SPEAKING HINDI]

1072
01:48:22,683 --> 01:48:24,337
You betrayed Siva!

1073
01:48:33,304 --> 01:48:34,660
[SCREAMING]

1074
01:48:56,105 --> 01:48:57,712
WILLIE: Well, it's about time.

1075
01:49:16,519 --> 01:49:17,924
MAN: Hold your fire.

1076
01:49:42,616 --> 01:49:44,020
[CHUCKLES]

1077
01:50:10,660 --> 01:50:15,011
[LAUGHING]

1078
01:50:33,359 --> 01:50:40,059
[ALL WHOOPING]

1079
01:50:41,201 --> 01:50:43,873
[EXCLAIMING EXCITEDLY]

1080
01:51:20,556 --> 01:51:22,729
We know you are coming back

1081
01:51:23,026 --> 01:51:25,674
when life return
to our village.

1082
01:51:29,915 --> 01:51:36,383
Now you can see the magic
of the rock you bring back.

1083
01:51:36,760 --> 01:51:40,097
Yes,
I understand its power now.

1084
01:51:46,234 --> 01:51:47,642
You could've kept it.

1085
01:51:47,830 --> 01:51:49,924
Ah! What for?
They'd just put it in a museum.

1086
01:51:50,012 --> 01:51:52,086
It'd be another rock
collecting dust.

1087
01:51:52,413 --> 01:51:55,136
But then it would've
given you your fortune and glory.

1088
01:51:55,883 --> 01:51:57,151
Anything could happen.

1089
01:51:57,718 --> 01:51:59,270
It's a long way to Delhi.

1090
01:51:59,987 --> 01:52:01,167
No, thanks.

1091
01:52:01,264 --> 01:52:03,424
No more adventures with you,
Dr. Jones.

1092
01:52:03,561 --> 01:52:06,776
Sweetheart, after all the fun
we've had together?

1093
01:52:08,309 --> 01:52:11,388
If you think I'm going to
Delhi with you, or anyplace else

1094
01:52:11,475 --> 01:52:13,435
after all the trouble
you've gotten me into,

1095
01:52:13,522 --> 01:52:15,219
think again, buster!

1096
01:52:15,296 --> 01:52:17,813
I'm going home to Missouri
where they never feed you snakes,

1097
01:52:17,930 --> 01:52:20,478
before ripping your heart out
and lowering you into hot pits!

1098
01:52:20,565 --> 01:52:23,747
This is not my idea
of a swell time!

1099
01:52:24,174 --> 01:52:27,426
Excuse me, sir.
I need a guide to Delhi. If you could...

1100
01:52:45,075 --> 01:52:46,175
[TRUMPETING]

1101
01:52:46,262 --> 01:52:48,296
[LAUGHING] Very funny.

1102
01:52:54,574 --> 01:52:55,782
Very funny.

1103
01:52:58,965 --> 01:53:00,221
Uh-oh!

1104
01:53:03,667 --> 01:53:07,749
[ALL CHEERING]

